#!/bin/bash
#
# boot the m16 hard disk image in the Decision 1 hardware simulator
#
# m16boot
#
# Runs d1 against the image install-hwsim builds.  The console and the
# debug terminal each get their own xterm, so this needs an X display.
#
# The image is disks/hdinstall/hddma-0, which is built - from scratch -
# by
#
#	make -C src/micronix install-hwsim
#
# which formats an m16, makes the filesystem, patches the kernel's root
# device, tars in the userland, and mknods the devices in /dev.  See
# src/micronix/GNUmakefile.inc for the recipe.
#

root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)

image="$root/disks/hdinstall/hddma-0"
d1="$root/src/hwsim/d1/d1"

if [ ! -x "$d1" ]; then
	echo "building d1 ..."
	make -C "$root/src/hwsim/d1"
fi

if [ ! -f "$image" ]; then
	echo "no image at $image" >&2
	echo "build it first: make -C $root/src/micronix install-hwsim" >&2
	exit 1
fi

# the simulator finds roms/mon447.bin and its resource files by being
# run from this directory
cd "$root/src/hwsim/d1" || exit 1

export TERMINAL_FONTSIZE="${TERMINAL_FONTSIZE:-14}"

# -c 0x10c, in the config switch bits:
#	0x100	uart 0 in an xterm (otherwise it wants the controlling tty)
#	0x08	boot the HDC-DMA controller (nuboot)
#	0x04	skip the monitor and boot straight away
# hdcdma0: is the drive - controller hdcdma, unit 0 - and the image.
"$d1" -b roms/mon447.bin -c 0x10c "hdcdma0:$image"

stty cooked echo echoe 2>/dev/null
